{
  "_note": "The effective per-route TBT budgets are in .github/lighthouse-budget.json (the CI action passes it as budgetsFile; its paths end in $ because a path without it also matches the longer paths: /ar would match /ar/c). This assertMatrix repeats the same numbers. TBT budget: 200 ms for /ar; /ar/consultations/doctors 230 ms; /ar/c 240 ms (measured 2026-10-23 on a production build, applied/devtools throttling as in CI; local runs reproduce the CI report). Cause found: a loading.tsx on a static/ISR page makes the cached HTML carry the skeleton plus a swap script, so the page hydrates twice; removed from /ar/consultations/doctors (313 -> 158-201 ms). /ar/c was above 200 because 24 generated client ProductCards hydrated on it (issue 1835): the grid is now server markup with only the add buttons as client code (components-next/pharmacy/product-card-static.tsx, add-to-cart-button.tsx), TBT median 392 -> 117 ms locally (3 runs each, same machine and stub catalogue), but 213 ms in the CI Lighthouse job (median of 3, one run of the job; before the change CI medians were 278-329): the 200 target is not reached in CI, so /ar/c is 240 (213 + a margin for the run-to-run spread) until the client CoreShell is also cut down. /ar/c keeps its loading.tsx: removing it passed 6 local runs (TTI 3.7-3.9 s) but the CI Lighthouse job on that commit failed with interactive 5707 ms against the 5500 budget, the same instability as in #1816. See docs/design/QUALITY_STANDARDS.md section 2.",
  "ci": {
    "collect": {
      "numberOfRuns": 3,
      "settings": {
        "throttlingMethod": "devtools"
      }
    },
    "assert": {
      "assertMatrix": [
        {
          "matchingUrlPattern": "^http://localhost:3000/ar$",
          "assertions": {
            "categories:performance": [
              "error",
              {
                "minScore": 0.9,
                "aggregationMethod": "median"
              }
            ],
            "categories:accessibility": [
              "error",
              {
                "minScore": 0.95,
                "aggregationMethod": "median"
              }
            ],
            "largest-contentful-paint": [
